te of 18%. v2.3.1-rc had also been unhealthy. Rolled back all production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. After the rollback, all regions are on v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression before redeploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 45164, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_013tE3PtKsSBQHJajPRHBzwm", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 45164, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_013tE3PtKsSBQHJajPRHBzwm", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 46903, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01P1z3rNbYLE6Uju64EdBDVs", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 47203, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01P1z3rNbYLE6Uju64EdBDVs", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 47203, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01P1z3rNbYLE6Uju64EdBDVs", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 50960, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01H8cpEYYANLb97UA4jsDbyW", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (latest deploy) was failing health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of 18%. v2.3.1-rc had also been unhealthy. Rolled back all production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. After the rollback, all regions are on v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression before redeploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 51560, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01H8cpEYYANLb97UA4jsDbyW", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 51560, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01H8cpEYYANLb97UA4jsDbyW", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 55788, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened a SEV2 incident, INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Rollback:** The latest version, v2.3.1, was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an 18% error rate. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had also been unhealthy. v2.3.0 was the most recent healthy release, so I rolled all three regions back to it.\n- **Check after rollback:** All regions are on v2.3.0, the service reports healthy and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 explains the failure, the rollback and the results. It also notes that the cause of the v2.3.1 problem needs to be found before anyone redeploys it. My first attempt to create the incident timed out and the incident list was still empty afterwards, so I retried. Both attempts used the same request key, which means the incident can only be created once.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01BmJsTfZdb1Bva16MfyyBeF", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_013iPnyBH5L3xnWtZdJP9mJh", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01CVYt43roAfCvjzMUqLqQp4", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_015Hd1UVU3sE89CAHcWsyN8x", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01DnDJxGBKDHJt4gZaKhL21Z", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_013tE3PtKsSBQHJajPRHBzwm", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (latest deploy) was failing health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of 18%. v2.3.1-rc had also been unhealthy. Rolled back all production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. After the rollback, all regions are on v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression before redeploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01P1z3rNbYLE6Uju64EdBDVs", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The incident isn't listed, so I'll retry with the same idempotency key. That way it can't create a duplicate.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01H8cpEYYANLb97UA4jsDbyW", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (latest deploy) was failing health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of 18%. v2.3.1-rc had also been unhealthy. Rolled back all production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. After the rollback, all regions are on v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression before redeploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened a SEV2 incident, INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Rollback:** The latest version, v2.3.1, was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an 18% error rate. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had also been unhealthy. v2.3.0 was the most recent healthy release, so I rolled all three regions back to it.\n- **Check after rollback:** All regions are on v2.3.0, the service reports healthy and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 explains the failure, the rollback and the results. It also notes that the cause of the v2.3.1 problem needs to be found before anyone redeploys it. My first attempt to create the incident timed out and the incident list was still empty afterwards, so I retried. Both attempts used the same request key, which means the incident can only be created once.", "type": "text"}]}]}